# stratonHub UI — Diataxis (Delta Only)
Applies on top of `00-global.always.mdc`. Do NOT restate global rules.

## UI Contract (Diataxis-first)
The UI must render documentation in exactly 4 modes:
- tutorial | how-to | reference | explanation

Each mode has a distinct layout + components. Do not mix modes.

## Required UI Components
- Surface Switcher: developers | business | users (always visible on desktop)
- Content Type Badge: tutorial/how-to/reference/explanation (always visible in header area)
- Breadcrumbs: must include surface + content type context
- TOC: required for reference + explanation; optional for tutorial/how-to

## Layout Rules by Diataxis Type
### Tutorial
- Must support step progression (next/prev)
- Optional progress indicator if steps exist
- Primary CTA: "Continue" / "Next step"
- Show prerequisites at top

### How-To
- Must be task-first (goal at top)
- Must display prerequisites + numbered steps
- Must include troubleshooting section slot
- Primary CTA: "Do the task"

### Reference
- Must optimize for lookup:
  - compact spacing, dense tables
  - copy-to-clipboard for code/commands
  - anchors for every section
- Prefer index/collapsible sections for long pages

### Explanation
- Must optimize for reading:
  - wider line-height and generous spacing
  - diagram slot supported
  - “related concepts” section slot

## Search UI (Cmd+K)
- Must support filters:
  - surface (dev/business/user)
  - type (tutorial/how-to/reference/explanation)
  - status (sealed/reviewed/draft)
- Ranking rule: sealed > reviewed > draft

## Accessibility (KISS)
- AA baseline always.
- Optional "Reading Accessibility Mode" toggle may adjust:
  - font size, line-height, contrast, focus ring visibility
- Do NOT promise AAA across every widget.

## Anti-Leak Discipline
- This rule applies ONLY to stratonHub UI files (app/components).
- Do not add globs outside `packages/stratonhub/`.
